Usage and error reports (TelemetryDeck, from v1.0-2026.11.12) are off in the Big Sur build unless turned on in
Settings ▸ General ▸ Share anonymous usage and error reports, where upstream sends them unless turned off; Help says so.
MetricKit's subscriber is macOS 12 (MXMetricManagerSubscriber, MXDiagnosticPayload), so Diagnostics is made and added
there only; on 11 the hang and CPU-spike reports don't exist. The classes are in 11.7's MetricKit, so the framework
loads.

